# Project Principles

- AI use increases capacity but does not transfer responsibility.
- Requirements definition and acceptance are part of engineering.
- Clarify consequential ambiguity before implementation.
- Define observable acceptance criteria and required evidence before claiming completion.
- Tests should verify system expectations and prevent meaningful regressions.
- Preserve traceability between requirements, decisions, implementation, tests, and release evidence.
- Prefer realistic inherited systems and continuing change over disposable prototypes.
- Treat security, performance, dependencies, operability, documentation, and handoff as product concerns.
- Revise the Definition of Done when experience exposes a missing or counterproductive practice.
- Do not declare work complete merely because code was generated, compiled, or demonstrated once.
